[Music]  you know the scene you know the story  for tim mcgraw and faith hill though it  was about way more than just playing  their parts their personal reaction to  what happens will blow you away  as the yellowstone universe continues to  expand the western drama's first  spin-off has wrapped its inaugural  season 1883 is a prequel to the  record-breaking series and chronicles  the dutton family's ancestors growling  journey from texas to montana before the  season came to an end it was announced  that more episodes would follow and fans  are already eager to see what comes  after the shocking finale episode 10  this is not your heaven sees the  dutton's eldest daughter elsa dutton  recovering from the arrow wound she  sustained in the previous episode many  1883 fans speculated that elsa would  survive the infection that began to set  in given that she is a main character  and the rapes are serious however the  finale proved this theory wrong despite  elsa's condition improving as a group  pushed forward on their long journey  things suddenly took a turn for the  worse drawing this is not your heaven  elsa must grapple with her doomed fate  and bid an emotional farewell to her  family by the end of the episode elsa  has succumbed to the infection declaring  she is unafraid before finally passing  away  that final father daughter scene was  clearly hard to watch for many and 1883  stars tim mcgraw and faith hill have  admitted that the entire episode was  difficult for them to shoot in an  interview with variety the real-life  couple opened up about the tragic death  of their on-screen daughter describing  the ark as one of the most incredible  stories she had ever read hill told the  publication as a mom i can't even allow  myself to go there i cannot it's really  hard even now to talk about because once  the tears start coming i can't stop them  i would tell the directors if we start  going it's going to be hard for me to  stop while james dutton gets to be with  elsa during her final moments margaret  must stay behind with her other children  watching helplessly as her daughter is  brought away to choose her final resting  place this scene in particular shook  hill during filming she told variety  imagine knowing that your child is going  to die and you cannot be by their side i  can't even imagine it ever i have not  recovered he went on to say that she  also cannot imagine how this loss will  affect james and margaret's marriage the  actress has been open about how 1883  takes an emotional toll on her noting  the death of her character's  sister-in-law earlier in the season  still makes her cry meanwhile tim mcgraw  told variety that when he read the last  scripts for season 1 of 1883 with hill  they couldn't stop crying he said  i mean ugly boo hoo crying i was a  blubbering idiot it was just so well  written so devastating and heartbreaking  but at the same time so on point and  poignant for what yellowstone turned out  to be mcgraw added it just gives you all  the reasons in the world where they  fight so hard for that land and why  their family fights so hard to keep what  they have it just made perfect sense no  matter how much sense it made though he  was still struck by elsa's death mcgraw  explained that he had to make an effort  not to get too emotional too early  during the scene but struggled because  isabelle may looks like she could be his  own daughter it's hard as a parent  playing that role you don't want to go  to any dark places in your mind about  your kid so you have to keep trying to  block that out and still be in the  moment with the character that you're  playing but the lines do get blurry  however he also agreed that this moment  played an important role in the greater  story even if fans aren't happy about it  mcgraw explained it's going to be a good  thing that they hate that ending because  it has to be that way and they know it  it's gonna be devastating why would you  watch stuff if it doesn't purge your  emotions  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

